ion","security"],"security-severity":"CRITICAL"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Improper neutralization of special elements in data query logic"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted input concatinated with raw SQL query can result in SQL Injection.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted input concatinated with raw SQL query can result in SQL Injection.\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-node_sqli_injection)\n","text":"Untrusted input concatinated with raw SQL query can result in SQL Injection.\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-node_sqli_injection","id":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-node_sqli_injection","name":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-node_sqli_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89","OWASP-A03:2021-Injection","OWASP-A1:2017-Injection","security"],"security-severity":"CRITICAL"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Improper neutralization of special elements used in an SQL command (SQL Injection)"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"'The Sequelize connection string indicates that database server does not use TLS. Non TLS connections are susceptible to man in the middle (MITM) attacks.'\n"},"help":{"markdown":"'The Sequelize connection string indicates that database server does not use TLS. Non TLS connections are susceptible to man in the middle (MITM) attacks.'\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls)\n","text":"'The Sequelize connection string indicates that database server does not use TLS. Non TLS connections are susceptible to man in the middle (MITM) attacks.'\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls","id":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls","name":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-319","OWASP-A02:2021-Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A3:2017-Sensitive Data Exposure","security"],"security-severity":"MEDIUM"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Cleartext transmission of sensitive information"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The Sequelize connection string indicates that TLS certificate validation \nof database server is disabled. This is equivalent to not having TLS. An \nattacker can present any invalid certificate and Sequelize will make database \nconnection ignoring certificate errors. This setting make the connection\nsusceptible to man in the middle (MITM) attacks. Not applicable to SQLite database.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The Sequelize connection string indicates that TLS certificate validation \nof database server is disabled. This is equivalent to not having TLS. An \nattacker can present any invalid certificate and Sequelize will make database \nconnection ignoring certificate errors. This setting make the connection\nsusceptible to man in the middle (MITM) attacks. Not applicable to SQLite database.\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls_cert_validation)\n","text":"The Sequelize connection string indicates that TLS certificate validation \nof database server is disabled. This is equivalent to not having TLS. An \nattacker can present any invalid certificate and Sequelize will make database \nconnection ignoring certificate errors. This setting make the connection\nsusceptible to man in the middle (MITM) attacks. Not applicable to SQLite database.\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls_cert_validation","id":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls_cert_validation","name":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_tls_cert_validation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-295","OWASP-A02:2021-Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A3:2017-Sensitive Data Exposure","security"],"security-severity":"HIGH"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Improper certificate validation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"'The Sequelize connection string indicates that an older version of TLS is in use. TLS1.0 and TLS1.1 are deprecated and should be used. By default, Sequelize use TLSv1.2 but it''s recommended to use TLS1.3. Not applicable to SQLite database.'\n"},"help":{"markdown":"'The Sequelize connection string indicates that an older version of TLS is in use. TLS1.0 and TLS1.1 are deprecated and should be used. By default, Sequelize use TLSv1.2 but it''s recommended to use TLS1.3. Not applicable to SQLite database.'\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_weak_tls)\n","text":"'The Sequelize connection string indicates that an older version of TLS is in use. TLS1.0 and TLS1.1 are deprecated and should be used. By default, Sequelize use TLSv1.2 but it''s recommended to use TLS1.3. Not applicable to SQLite database.'\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_weak_tls","id":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_weak_tls","name":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-database-rule-sequelize_weak_tls","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-757","OWASP-A02:2021-Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A3:2017-Sensitive Data Exposure","security"],"security-severity":"CRITICAL"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Selection of Less-Secure Algorithm During Negotiation (Algorithm Downgrade)"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"This application is looping over user controlled objects, which can lead to a layer 7 denial of service vulnerability.\n\nA layer 7 denial of service attack refers to overloading the application layer of the OSI model, typically layer 7. \nThis can happen when user-controlled input such as objects, arrays, strings, etc. are iterated or looped over without proper validation or limits in place.\n\nFor example, if a user can control the size of an array or object passed into the application, \nthey could create an extremely large input that gets looped over. This would consume excessive CPU cycles or memory, \npotentially crashing or slowing down the application.\n\nTo prevent this, limits should be set on the number of iterations, input sizes, recursion depth, etc.\n\nSample case of secure array looped over with user-controlled input\n```\n// Potential DoS if req.body.list.length is large.\napp.post('/dos/layer7-object-dos/for-loop/1', function (req, res) {\n    var list = req.body.list;\n    for (let i = 0; i <= 10; i++) {\n        if(!list[i]){\n          // return;\n        }  \n    }\n    res.send(\"res\")\n});\n```\n\nImplementing protections against layer 7 denial of service attacks is important for securing modern web applications and APIs.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"This application is looping over user controlled objects, which can lead to a layer 7 denial of service vulnerability.\n\nA layer 7 denial of service attack refers to overloading the application layer of the OSI model, typically layer 7. \nThis can happen when user-controlled input such as objects, arrays, strings, etc. are iterated or looped over without proper validation or limits in place.\n\nFor example, if a user can control the size of an array or object passed into the application, \nthey could create an extremely large input that gets looped over. This would consume excessive CPU cycles or memory, \npotentially crashing or slowing down the application.\n\nTo prevent this, limits should be set on the number of iterations, input sizes, recursion depth, etc.\n\nSample case of secure array looped over with user-controlled input\n```\n// Potential DoS if req.body.list.length is large.\napp.post('/dos/layer7-object-dos/for-loop/1', function (req, res) {\n    var list = req.body.list;\n    for (let i = 0; i <= 10; i++) {\n        if(!list[i]){\n          // return;\n        }  \n    }\n    res.send(\"res\")\n});\n```\n\nImplementing protections against layer 7 denial of service attacks is important for securing modern web applications and APIs.\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-layer7_object_dos)\n","text":"This application is looping over user controlled objects, which can lead to a layer 7 denial of service vulnerability.\n\nA layer 7 denial of service attack refers to overloading the application layer of the OSI model, typically layer 7. \nThis can happen when user-controlled input such as objects, arrays, strings, etc. are iterated or looped over without proper validation or limits in place.\n\nFor example, if a user can control the size of an array or object passed into the application, \nthey could create an extremely large input that gets looped over. This would consume excessive CPU cycles or memory, \npotentially crashing or slowing down the application.\n\nTo prevent this, limits should be set on the number of iterations, input sizes, recursion depth, etc.\n\nSample case of secure array looped over with user-controlled input\n```\n// Potential DoS if req.body.list.length is large.\napp.post('/dos/layer7-object-dos/for-loop/1', function (req, res) {\n    var list = req.body.list;\n    for (let i = 0; i <= 10; i++) {\n        if(!list[i]){\n          // return;\n        }  \n    }\n    res.send(\"res\")\n});\n```\n\nImplementing protections against layer 7 denial of service attacks is important for securing modern web applications and APIs.\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-layer7_object_dos","id":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-layer7_object_dos","name":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-layer7_object_dos","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-400","OWASP-A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A6:2017-Security Misconfiguration","security"],"security-severity":"MEDIUM"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Uncontrolled resource consumption"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Ensure that the regex used to compare with user supplied input is safe from regular expression denial of service.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Ensure that the regex used to compare with user supplied input is safe from regular expression denial of service.\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-regex_dos)\n","text":"Ensure that the regex used to compare with user supplied input is safe from regular expression denial of service.\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-regex_dos","id":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-regex_dos","name":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-dos-rule-regex_dos","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-185","OWASP-A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A6:2017-Security Misconfiguration","security"],"security-severity":"MEDIUM"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Incorrect regular expression"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Application can load content over HTTP and that makes the app vulnerable to Man in the middle attacks.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Application can load content over HTTP and that makes the app vulnerable to Man in the middle attacks.\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-electronjs-rule-electron_allow_http)\n","text":"Application can load content over HTTP and that makes the app vulnerable to Man in the middle attacks.\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-electronjs-rule-electron_allow_http","id":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-electronjs-rule-electron_allow_http","name":"gitlab.nodejs_scan.javascript-electronjs-rule-electron_allow_http","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-319","OWASP-A05:2021-Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A6:2017-Security Misconfiguration","security"],"security-severity":"CRITICAL"},"shortDescription":{"text":"Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Blink's expirimental features are enabled in this application. Some of the features may affect the security of the application.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Blink's expirimental features are enabled in this application. Some of the features may affect the security of the application.\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgr